I actually have a little experience with this situation.  When I got the Velious version I upgraded right away and was ready to tackle the new world.  I went to North Ro, waited patiently for the raft to come pick me up, got on the raft, waited forever for the raft to finally start to move, then "LOADING PLEASE WAIT..."  Oh the excitement of all the new Phat L00t just waiting for me!  As the new wonderful world of Velious was loading on my computer I had to quick run into the kitchen to grab the microwaved feast that was to be my dinner.  Come back from the kitchen and Shato standing in the middle of a new and strange desert land no where near water.  What the heck?  Well, its a new world, so I figured either its supposed to happen that way (unlikely), or more likely it was a bug that they haven't worked out yet (yeah that's got to be it).  Well, hopefully this isn't a dangerous place for necros, and maybe I'll have gotten lucky and be standing by some cool new mob or something.  Anyway, after catiously checking out the nearby new mobs and everything, I quickly started to get a strong feeling of dejavu.  Hmmmm, Dune Tarantulas, Orc Warriors, hey, there is some Noob shouting about Born D'Vinn...  Wait a second...  After a quick check of the scroll back buffer the problem was solved:<BR>"LOADING PLEASE WAIT..."<BR>Your version of EverQuest does not support Velious blah blah blah.<P>So I ended up at the safe point in North Ro.  So my guess is, if you gated one of two things is going to happen.  You'll end up at the safe point in North Ro (kind of doubt that) or more likely you'll end up at the safe point of your current zone.<P>Ya know, either one of those could be exploited.  I guess the NRo option would be the least likely to be exploited, but if you end up at the safe point in your current zone, think how cool that would be as a tank class.  Bind in Velious, get a port back to the old world, switch accounts to a non-Velious, then whenever you die, instead of going to Velious you go to your current zone's safe point.  You'd never need a bind your whole life...
